    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_11b8a87a",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image features a Black man, likely actor Michael B. Jordan, in a posed, serious stance, overlaid with text that reads: 'until you give the white man back his god, everything i post is going to offend you.' This text is a direct, confrontational, and racially charged statement that frames the speaker's expression of identity or critique as inherently offensive to white people, implying that white people are entitled to a specific religious or cultural narrative. The meme uses the image of a Black man to visually represent the speaker, and the text is designed to provoke a reaction by suggesting that any expression of Black identity or critique will be seen as offensive by white audiences. This is a hateful message because it targets individuals based on race, implying that their expression is inherently offensive and that they are responsible for the discomfort of white people. The meme is not merely humorous or ironic; it is a direct attack on the racial dynamics of expression and offense, and it promotes the idea that Black people are inherently disruptive to white cultural norms. The overall intent is to provoke outrage or discomfort by framing the speaker's identity as a source of offense, which is a form of racialized hate speech.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_9290c406"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
